PIPEFS: read() at end of file returns 0 instead of failing with EAGAIN

A PIPEFS read of an empty pipe failed with EAGAIN even once every write
end had closed, while poll() already reported POLLHUP there, so a reader
that polled and read until end of file spun on EAGAIN instead. Return 0
when the pipe is empty and its writers have closed.

Upstream: https://github.com/emscripten-core/emscripten/issues/26708 (open)
Draft: docs/upstream/emscripten-pipe-read-eof.md

diff --git a/src/lib/libpipefs.js b/src/lib/libpipefs.js
index 05b8295..f694f08 100644
--- a/src/lib/libpipefs.js
+++ b/src/lib/libpipefs.js
@@ -168,6 +168,10 @@ addToLibrary({
           return 0;
         }
         if (currentLength == 0) {
+          // With every write end closed the pipe is at EOF.
+          if (pipe.writeClosed) {
+            return 0;
+          }
           // Behave as if the read end is always non-blocking
           throw new FS.ErrnoError({{{ cDefs.EAGAIN }}});
         }
